 most serious type of skin  cancer there are other types of skin  cancer as well but it melanoma is the  most serious type of skin cancer and as  you can see in this picture it will look  something similar to this  initially you might think of it as a  mole but it when it starts spreading  uh it obviously would not look like a  mole anymore  so melanoma is basically  the most serious kind of  skin cancer and  one of the risk factors that i told you  is having a fairer skin  yes if you have a fairer skin the  chances of you developing melanoma is  very high so it is one of those risk  factors risk factor  we all know risk factor basically means  anything that would increase your chance  of having that particular disease thus  having a fairer skin  would  increase your chance of developing  melanoma  so  now that we've learned about melanin and  melanoma let us  talk about our topic that is about the  transcriptomic  analysis of the role of the melanin in  melanoma  so  if i talk about the human epidermal  melanocytes or the hems  they provide a critical protection  against the skin cancer  um again skin cancer are of different  types but here we'll talk about uh  melanoma  uh it protects us against the sunburns  and photo aging so they definitely play  a very important role in  skin cancer or melanoma  so in this  research project i took two samples  uh from the darker skin people and two  from the lighter skin people and then  compared them  to understand about the different genes  that are expressed in the darker skin  and lighter skin and as i discussed  earlier that the darker skin people  would be having more melanin production  in them  thus their chance of developing skin  cancer is lesser  and the lighter skin would be having  very less melanin production in them  thus their  chance of developing  skin cancer or melanoma would be higher  so this was the basis of my study this  was the basis on which i started about  my research  project  now if i talk about t